font-semibold tracking-[-0.028em] text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.6vw,2.5rem)]","children":"The pieces"}],null]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-7 lg:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","div","Storage",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Storage"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"One columnar store of wide events. A log line is a span with no duration, so logs and spans share a table — storing them apart is what makes correlation a human activity rather than a query. Metrics are separate, because they arrive pre-aggregated and are queried by series over time."}]]}],["$","div","Tenancy",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Tenancy"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"The workspace is the first expression in every sort key and partition key. Tenancy is a physical property of the storage, not a predicate the query builder has to remember: a query that omits it reads nothing rather than reading everyone."}]]}],["$","div","Ingestion",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Ingestion"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"OTLP over HTTP and gRPC. Each batch is authenticated, placed, validated, redacted, checked against the cardinality budget, sampled, enriched with deployment context, metered and written. Refusals are recorded with the series or attribute at fault."}]]}],["$","div","Enrichment",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Enrichment"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Deployment, image digest, build and commit are stamped at ingest from the platform's own records. They are never read from telemetry attributes, which the sending workload controls."}]]}],["$","div","Cardinality",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Cardinality"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Budgets are per workspace and count-based. An over-budget series is refused by name and surfaced in the portal the same day, rather than dropped quietly or billed silently."}]]}],["$","div","Query",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Query"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"PromQL for the supported query set, log and trace search, and read-only SQL. Every query is costed before it runs and refused with an estimate if it exceeds the workspace ceiling."}]]}],["$","div","Correlation",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Correlation"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Deterministic, not statistical. Candidate changes are ranked by temporal proximity, affected service, shared deployment and image change. No claim is made that this is machine learning, because it is not."}]]}],["$","div","eBPF and Kubernetes",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"eBPF and Kubernetes"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Where Cilium and Hubble are present, flow data contributes service relationships and network telemetry. Feature detection decides whether the integration is enabled; its absence degrades the collector rather than breaking it."}]]}],["$","div","Retention",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Retention"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Configurable per environment and applied by the storage engine's TTL rather than by a sweep job."}]]}],["$","div","Export",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[15px] font-semibold","children":"Export"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Query APIs, result export, and a cold tier designed around open columnar formats so telemetry stays readable outside ClueLake."}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"$undefined","className":"py-16 sm:py-24 border-t border-[color:var(--color-line)]","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1160px] px-5 sm:px-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[46rem]","children":[null,["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-3 font-semibold tracking-[-0.028em] text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.6vw,2.5rem)]","children":"Sending telemetry"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","children":"Standard OTLP. No proprietary agent is required."}]]}],["$","$L8",null,{"className":"mt-6 max-w-[46rem]","label":"otel-collector-config.yaml","code":"exporters:\n  otlphttp/cluelake:\n    endpoint: ${CLUELAKE_ENDPOINT}\n    headers:\n      authorization: Bearer ${CLUELAKE_INGEST_TOKEN}\n\nservice:\n  pipelines:\n    traces:  { exporters: [otlphttp/cluelake] }\n    metrics: { exporters: [otlphttp/cluelake] }\n    logs:    { exporters: [otlphttp/cluelake] }"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"grid-field border-t border-[color:var(--color-line)] py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1160px] px-5 sm:px-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[40rem]","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-[clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.1rem)] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em]","children":"Stop asking what broke."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-[clamp(1.25rem,2.6vw,1.75rem)] text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]","child